ia"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/19806"} "22 from 22 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Two single-elimination pools, with winner of each pool advanced to the final. All judoka losing to the finalists in each pool advanced to repêchage pools, with the winners of the repêchage pools earning bronze medals."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The last two World Championships had been won by the last two Olympic champions, both Chinese " [:em {} "judoka"] ". " [:a {:href "/athletes/33323"} "Sun Fuming"] " was Olympic gold medalist in 1996 and World Champion in 2003, while " [:a {:href "/athletes/92260"} "Yuan Hua"] " was Olympic gold medalist in 2000 and World Champion in 2001. Only one could represent China in the class, and Sun was chosen. She went to the A Pool final, where she faced Cuba’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/92270"} "Daima Beltrán"] ", the silver medalist in 2000, with Beltrán winning by " [:em {} "ippon"] " in 1:39. The other pool was won by Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/106473"} "Maki Tsukada"] ", who had been runner-up at the 2003 Worlds. Beltrán got off fast in the final, throwing Tsukuda for " [:em {} "waza-ari"] ", but at 1:50, Tsukuda pinned Beltrán for " [:em {} "ippon"] " to win the gold medal, leaving Beltrán with her second consecutive silver. Tsukuda would return in 2008 to win a silver medal in the class in Beijing, after winning the 2007 World Championship in the open class."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/106473"} "Maki Tsukada"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style "